This new implementation is less than half the code (+187, -389) and avoids creating work for the optimizer in quite a lot of places.

- Before: https://gist.github.com/rust-play/d5ea8b992cc58ef0968eaa158ad01902 + https://gist.github.com/rust-play/cdf5e8a4e8572d52df9706854edfc7fa

- After: https://gist.github.com/rust-play/de44c2234c4380418d95464424cef427

For example compare what happens when deserializing an `i8` via `visit_i8`. Before:

```rust
            #[inline]
            fn visit_i8<E>(self, v: i8) -> Result<Self::Value, E>
            where
                E: Error,
            {
                match FromPrimitive::from_i8(v) {
                    Some(v) => Ok(v),
                    None => Err(Error::invalid_value(Unexpected::Signed(v as i64), &self)),
                }
            }
...
    impl FromPrimitive for i8 {
        #[inline]
        fn from_i8(n: i8) -> Option<Self> {
            if i8::min_value() as i64 <= n as i64 && n as i64 <= i8::max_value() as i64 {
                Some(n as i8)
            } else {
                None
            }
        }
        ...
    }
```

After:

```rust
            #[inline]
            fn visit_i8<E>(self, v: i8) -> Result<Self::Value, E>
            where
                E: Error,
            {
                Ok(v)
            }
```

## Proposed Change:

Add the new prop `interactOptions` which allows customisation of `interactjs`

This prop is an object with 3 possible keys,

`pointerEvents`: Allow setting custom `interactjs.pointEvents` options
`draggable`: Allow setting custom `interactjs.draggable` options
`resizable`: Allow setting custom `interactjs.resizable` options

Example usage

```
const interactOptions = {
  pointerEvents: {
    ignoreFrom: '[no-pointer-event]', // Prevent the item selected callbacks when clicking on these elements
  },
  resizable: {
    cursorChecker (action) { // Use custom cursors
      if (action.edges.left) { return 'w-resize'}
      if (action.edges.right) { return 'e-resize'}
    }
  }
}

<Timeline {...props} interactOptions={interactOptions}/>
```

